      "message": "The bcdDevice and power changes look OK.\n\nI don\u0027t get the AMA changes, including setting `Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter` to true, filling out the AMA fields, and specifying Discover SVIDs/Modes responses for TBT3 and DPAM. At one point, the VIF spec required that a TBT3 DFP (which the DUT is) also specify that it was a TBT3 UFP and therefore AMA (which the DUT is not intended to be). That requirement was removed in VIF spec 3.33. There is no such requirement for DPAM, and I don\u0027t think it\u0027s possible for the port to act as a UFP_D.\n\nIf these VIF updates accurately reflect the behavior during testing, we should probably be talking about the firmware changes instead of the VIF changes.",
